@startuml activity-diagram
' ============================================================================
' COLORS Web Application - Activity Diagram
' Repository: WilsonVu/ColorsLab
' Swimlanes show where each step runs: the person, the browser (HTML pages and
' js/code.js), the PHP endpoints in api/, and the MySQL database.
' Render with PlantUML (VS Code or IntelliJ PlantUML plugin, or
' https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml).
' Action colours follow the lanes: blue = Browser, violet = PHP API,
' green = MySQL (the same colours as the SVG/PDF versions).
' ============================================================================

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam titleFontSize 20
skinparam titleFontStyle bold
skinparam ArrowColor #334155
skinparam ArrowFontColor #64748B
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
' Uncomment to use the same font as the SVG/PDF versions (if Inter is installed):
' skinparam defaultFontName Inter

skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #64748B
  StartColor #1E293B
  EndColor #1E293B
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  DiamondBorderColor #1E293B
}
skinparam swimlane {
  BorderColor #94A3B8
  TitleFontStyle bold
  TitleFontSize 14
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FEFCE8
  BorderColor #CA8A04
  FontSize 11
}

title COLORS Web Application - Activity Diagram
caption Log in, search and add colors, log out. Derived from public/*.html, public/js/code.js and api/*.php

' ================================================================ LOG IN ===
|User|
start
:Open the COLORS website;
|Browser|
#EFF6FF:Load **index.html** and show the log-in form;
|User|
repeat
  :Type username and password,\nthen click **Do It**;
  |Browser|
  #EFF6FF:**doLogin()**: POST {login, password}\nto Login.php;
  note right
Every call in code.js is an asynchronous
XMLHttpRequest POST with a JSON body. The
page reacts only when the reply has status 200.
  end note
  |PHP API|
  #F5F3FF:**Login.php**: decode the JSON body,\nrun a prepared SELECT;
  note right
Every PHP script opens its own mysqli
connection to MySQL on localhost. If that
fails, it replies with the error message.
  end note
  |MySQL|
  #ECFDF5:SELECT ID, firstName, lastName\nFROM Users WHERE Login = ?\nAND Password = ?;
  |PHP API|
  #F5F3FF:Reply {id, firstName, lastName, error}\nid = 0 if no row matches;
  |Browser|
  if (id < 1?) then (yes)
    #EFF6FF:Show "User/Password\ncombination incorrect";
  else (no)
    #EFF6FF:**saveCookie()**: firstName, lastName,\nuserId, cookie expires in 20 min;
    #EFF6FF:Go to **color.html**, on page load\nit calls **readCookie()**;
    if (userId found in cookie?) then (yes)
    else (no)
      #EFF6FF:Redirect to **index.html**;
    endif
  endif
repeat while (logged in with a session?) is (no)
->yes;

' =========================================================== COLORS PAGE ===
|User|
repeat
  :Type a color or search text, then\nclick **Search Color**, **Add Color** or **Log Out**;
  if (Search Color clicked?) then (yes)
    ' ------------------------------------------------------------ search ---
    |Browser|
    #EFF6FF:**searchColor()**: POST {search, userId}\nto SearchColors.php;
    |PHP API|
    #F5F3FF:**SearchColors.php**: build the\npattern "%" + search + "%";
    |MySQL|
    #ECFDF5:SELECT Name FROM Colors\nWHERE Name LIKE ?\nAND UserID = ?;
    |PHP API|
    #F5F3FF:Reply {results: [names], error: ~""}\nif none: error "No Records Found"\nand no results array;
    note right
No match: the reply has no results array,
so searchColor() stops at results.length
and the old list stays on screen.
    end note
    |Browser|
    if (results in reply?) then (yes)
      #EFF6FF:Show the matching names\nin #colorList, one per line;
    else (no)
      #EFF6FF:Leave #colorList unchanged\n(old results stay on screen);
    endif
  elseif (Add Color clicked?) then (yes)
    ' --------------------------------------------------------------- add ---
    |Browser|
    #EFF6FF:**addColor()**: POST {color, userId}\nto AddColor.php;
    |PHP API|
    #F5F3FF:**AddColor.php**: decode the JSON body,\nrun a prepared INSERT;
    |MySQL|
    #ECFDF5:INSERT INTO Colors\n(UserId, Name) VALUES (?, ?);
    |PHP API|
    #F5F3FF:Reply {error: ~""};
    |Browser|
    #EFF6FF:Show "Color has been added"\n(the error field is not checked);
  else (Log Out clicked)
  endif
repeat while (Log Out clicked?) is (no)
->yes;

' =============================================================== LOG OUT ===
|Browser|
#EFF6FF:**doLogout()**: reset userId and names,\nexpire the cookie;
#EFF6FF:Redirect to **index.html**;
stop

@enduml
